# Byteman rule for internode_application_send_queue_capacity-acquireCapacity-pendingCapacityInBytes, case 9c: the trigger (amended 2026-10-07).
# At the entry of LargeMessageDelivery.doRun the delivery thread PARKS inside stage4.Hold.park while the file named by -Dstage4.hold.file exists,
# so nothing is polled or serialized and pending bytes only accumulate. Removing the file releases the same invocation, which then polls and drains the queue.
# NOT "RETURN false": that would stop the link and, at the plateau, nothing could start it again (9a logic step 7).
# stage4.Hold is compiled into a jar on the boot class path (-Xbootclasspath/a:) by cluster-run.py. Loaded on the sending node S only.
# One line when a thread parks and one when it is released, to the file named by -Dstage4.byteman.out:
#   hold park thread=<name> file=<path> ms=<epoch>      /      hold release ...

RULE hold large delivery
CLASS org.apache.cassandra.net.OutboundConnection$LargeMessageDelivery
METHOD doRun
AT ENTRY
IF stage4.Hold.held(java.lang.System.getProperty("stage4.hold.file"))
DO traceOpen("ssq", java.lang.System.getProperty("stage4.byteman.out", "send.trace"));
   traceln("ssq", "hold park thread=" + java.lang.Thread.currentThread().getName() + " file=" + java.lang.System.getProperty("stage4.hold.file") + " ms=" + java.lang.System.currentTimeMillis());
   stage4.Hold.park(java.lang.System.getProperty("stage4.hold.file"));
   traceln("ssq", "hold release thread=" + java.lang.Thread.currentThread().getName() + " ms=" + java.lang.System.currentTimeMillis())
ENDRULE
